# Smart Irrigation Monitoring & AI Decision Dashboard Implementation

## User Review Required
No immediate user review required, proceeding with standard UI dashboard layout per requirements.

## Proposed Changes

### Python API
#### [MODIFY] main.py (farmer_ai-python)
- Add `SmartIrrigationRequest` Pydantic model for receiving `temperature`, `humidity`, `soil_moisture`, and `water_flow`.
- Add `@app.post("/predict/smart-irrigation")` endpoint implementing the exact AI logic:
  - `< 40%` soil moisture = irrigation needed.
  - `40-60%` = not required.
  - `> 60%` = OFF.
  - Return `irrigation_needed`, `duration` (in seconds), and `confidence`.

### Node API
#### [NEW] iotRoutes.js (farmer_ai-backend/src/routes/)
#### [NEW] iotController.js (farmer_ai-backend/src/controllers/)
- Implement `POST /api/iot/sensor-data` to act as a webhook for future ESP32 integration. It will broadcast or store real-time data.

### Frontend
#### [MODIFY] Sidebar.jsx (farmer_ai-frontend/src/components/dashboard/)
- Add a new "Smart Irrigation" navigation link with a Droplet icon, pointing to `/smart-irrigation`.

#### [MODIFY] App.jsx (farmer_ai-frontend/src/)
- Add routing for `<Route path="/smart-irrigation" element={<SmartIrrigationDashboard />} />`.

#### [NEW] SmartIrrigationDashboard.jsx (farmer_ai-frontend/src/pages/)
- Create the main dashboard component meeting all 8 user requirements:
  1. Live Sensor Data Panel (Temp, Humidity, Soil Moisture, Flow).
  2. AI Irrigation Recommendation Panel (Status, Duration, Confidence).
  3. Pump Status Panel (ON / OFF).
  4. Data Visualization using Recharts (Soil Moisture Trend, Temp/Humidity Trend, Water Usages, Timeline).
  5. Mock Data Mode (runs interval every 5 seconds to generate data if real data isn't arriving).
  6. Visual Indicators (Green/Yellow/Red for Soil Moisture).
  7. Pump control simulation (calculating estimated water usage and duration).

## Verification Plan
### Automated Verification
- Backend nodes start correctly.
- Python server starts correctly.
### Manual Verification
- View `/smart-irrigation` in browser.
- Verify that every 5 seconds a new data point is generated and plotted.
- Verify AI logic is correct (pump turns ON when soil < 40%).
- Verify visual indicators match specifications.
